{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-39636","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43996","text":"Graphonomous × box-and-box — Arithmetic Compliance Review"}]},{"id":"blk-39637","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43997","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-43998","text":" review (no behavior change) · "},{"id":"spn-43999","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-44000","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44001","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-44002","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-44003","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-44004","text":" how closely the Graphonomous memory engine (OS-001) already conforms to the [&] governance kernel, rung by rung, and the small set of *additive* naming/wiring changes that would make it explicitly compliant."}]},{"id":"blk-39638","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44005","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-39639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44006","text":"Graphonomous is "},{"id":"spn-44007","marks":["bold"],"text":"already structurally isomorphic"},{"id":"spn-44008","text":" to the kernel's load-bearing rungs — it just doesn't *name* them. Its coverage→decision policy is the bridge ("},{"id":"spn-44009","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-44010","text":"); its coverage score is the axiological semiring; its Wilson intervals are the epistemic rung; its cost cap is the resource rung's affine ledger. The gap is "},{"id":"spn-44011","marks":["bold"],"text":"vocabulary + two small guarantees"},{"id":"spn-44012","text":", not architecture. Nothing here requires a core refactor; every recommendation is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-39640","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44013","text":"Compliance scorecard"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39642","spans":[{"id":"spn-44014","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-39643","spans":[{"id":"spn-44015","text":"Graphonomous implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-39644","spans":[{"id":"spn-44016","text":"Compliance"}]}],"id":"blk-39641","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39645","spans":[{"id":"spn-44017","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-44018","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-44019","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-39646","spans":[{"id":"spn-44020","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology.compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-44021","text":", SCC analysis; node confidence"}]},{"id":"blk-39647","spans":[{"id":"spn-44022","text":"✅ ~90% — κ is a first-class Value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39648","spans":[{"id":"spn-44023","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-44024","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-44025","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-39649","spans":[{"id":"spn-44026","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-44027","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44028","marks":["code"],"text":"Reranker"}]},{"id":"blk-39650","spans":[{"id":"spn-44029","text":"◻ ~60% — weighted sum, not a *named* semiring"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39651","spans":[{"id":"spn-44030","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-39652","spans":[{"id":"spn-44031","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-44032","text":" floor gates (act/learn/escalate)"}]},{"id":"blk-39653","spans":[{"id":"spn-44033","text":"◻ ~70% — floor present, "},{"id":"spn-44034","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-44035","text":" veto implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39654","spans":[{"id":"spn-44036","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-39655","spans":[{"id":"spn-44037","text":"consolidation cadence; freshness/staleness decay"}]},{"id":"blk-39656","spans":[{"id":"spn-44038","text":"◻ ~40% — time-aware, no LTL obligations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39657","spans":[{"id":"spn-44039","text":"5. reflexive (entrenched ring-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-39658","spans":[{"id":"spn-44040","text":"— (no self-amendment surface)"}]},{"id":"blk-39659","spans":[{"id":"spn-44041","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39660","spans":[{"id":"spn-44042","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-39661","spans":[{"id":"spn-44043","marks":["code"],"text":"Uncertainty.interval/1"},{"id":"spn-44044","text":" (Wilson), "},{"id":"spn-44045","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-44046","text":" (AGM)"}]},{"id":"blk-39662","spans":[{"id":"spn-44047","text":"✅ ~95% — strongest rung"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39663","spans":[{"id":"spn-44048","text":"7. strategic (coalition power)"}]},{"id":"blk-39664","spans":[{"id":"spn-44049","text":"— (single-agent; delegated to Deliberatic)"}]},{"id":"blk-39665","spans":[{"id":"spn-44050","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39666","spans":[{"id":"spn-44051","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-39667","spans":[{"id":"spn-44052","marks":["code"],"text":"CostTracker.budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-44053","text":" ($10/day), "},{"id":"spn-44054","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-44055","text":" LRU+decay"}]},{"id":"blk-39668","spans":[{"id":"spn-44056","text":"◻ ~85% — ledger present"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-39669","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44057","text":"Rung-by-rung detail (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-39670","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44058","text":"Rung 1 — alethic ("},{"id":"spn-44059","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-44060","text":") ✅"}]},{"id":"blk-39671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44061","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/topology.ex"},{"id":"spn-44062","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44063","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-44064","text":" (line 134) computes the "},{"id":"spn-44065","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ cyclicity invariant"},{"id":"spn-44066","text":" — the same Value-family invariant the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-44067","marks":["code"],"text":"value.mjs"},{"id":"spn-44068","text":" carries (alethic \"what can happen\"). Node confidence scores are the truth-degrees over which Value laws "},{"id":"spn-44069","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-44070","text":" range. "},{"id":"spn-44071","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-44072","text":"; recommend citing the rung-1 correspondence in the "},{"id":"spn-44073","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology"},{"id":"spn-44074","text":" moduledoc so κ is understood as the alethic Value, not a bespoke metric."}]},{"id":"blk-39672","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44075","text":"Rung 2 — axiological ("},{"id":"spn-44076","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-44077","text":") ◻ → name the semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-39673","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44078","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-44079","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44080","marks":["code"],"text":"weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-44081","text":" (line 604) computes "},{"id":"spn-44082","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ value × weight"},{"id":"spn-44083","text":" and clamps to "},{"id":"spn-44084","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,1]"},{"id":"spn-44085","text":". That is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-44086","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-44087","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-44088","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-44089","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44090","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-44091","text":") from "},{"id":"spn-44092","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-44093","text":". "},{"id":"spn-44094","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-44095","text":" document that the coverage score *is* the axiological rung in the probability semiring, and (optionally) expose a tropical ("},{"id":"spn-44096","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-44097","text":") \"weakest-component\" view alongside the weighted mean — so the engine can answer \"is any coverage component failing?\" the way the kernel's safety floor does, not just \"how good on average?\"."}]},{"id":"blk-39674","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44098","text":"Rung 3 — deontic (norm/govern) ◻ → make the "},{"id":"spn-44099","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-44100","text":" veto explicit"}]},{"id":"blk-39675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44101","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-44102","text":" (line 392) is "},{"id":"spn-44103","marks":["bold"],"text":"the bridge, already implemented"},{"id":"spn-44104","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-39676","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":act  when coverage ≥ floor  AND uncertainty ≤ ceiling  AND risk ≤ ceiling   # feasible ▸ permitted\n:learn when (looser floor)                                                    # permitted, not yet best\n:escalate otherwise                                                           # floor not met"},{"id":"blk-39677","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44105","text":"This is exactly "},{"id":"spn-44106","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-44107","text":": the conjunctive thresholds are the "},{"id":"spn-44108","marks":["bold"],"text":"un-weakenable safety floor"},{"id":"spn-44109","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-44110","marks":["code"],"text":"decision_confidence/3"},{"id":"spn-44111","text":" (line 409) is the "},{"id":"spn-44112","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-44113","text":" that the bridge's "},{"id":"spn-44114","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-44115","text":" step optimizes. The one missing guarantee is "},{"id":"spn-44116","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-44117","text":": in the kernel, a floor violation *annihilates* the verdict (no amount of gradient can rescue it). Graphonomous approximates this — "},{"id":"spn-44118","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-44119","text":" is terminal — but the relationship is implicit. "},{"id":"spn-44120","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-44121","text":" state in the "},{"id":"spn-44122","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage"},{"id":"spn-44123","text":" moduledoc that a sub-floor signal annihilates to "},{"id":"spn-44124","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-44125","text":" (the deontic "},{"id":"spn-44126","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-44127","text":"), and add a property test mirroring the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-44128","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-44129","text":" annihilation law so the guarantee can't silently regress."}]},{"id":"blk-39678","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44130","text":"Rung 4 — temporal (LTL ▸ supervise) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-39679","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44131","text":"Freshness/staleness decay ("},{"id":"spn-44132","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-44133","text":" line 383) and consolidation cadence are time-aware, but there are no explicit LTL obligations (e.g. \"every stored contradiction is *eventually* resolved\"). "},{"id":"spn-44134","marks":["bold"],"text":"Out of scope to add now"},{"id":"spn-44135","text":"; flagged as the natural next rung if temporal guarantees become first-class. Maps to "},{"id":"spn-44136","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/temporal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-44137","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-44138","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-44139","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44140","marks":["code"],"text":"◇"},{"id":"spn-44141","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-39680","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44142","text":"Rung 6 — epistemic (knows ▸ believes) ✅ strongest"}]},{"id":"blk-39681","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44143","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/uncertainty.ex"},{"id":"spn-44144","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44145","marks":["code"],"text":"interval/1"},{"id":"spn-44146","text":" (line 28) computes "},{"id":"spn-44147","marks":["bold"],"text":"Wilson confidence intervals"},{"id":"spn-44148","text":" over evidence counts, with an explicit "},{"id":"spn-44149","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-44150","text":" bottom — this is the kernel's epistemic rung (S5/KD45 \"knows ▸ believes\") in statistical form. "},{"id":"spn-44151","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-44152","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-44153","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGM"},{"id":"spn-44154","text":" expansion/contraction with "},{"id":"spn-44155","marks":["code"],"text":"contradicts"},{"id":"spn-44156","text":" edges. "},{"id":"spn-44157","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-44158","text":" at ~95%; recommend naming the "},{"id":"spn-44159","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-44160","text":" case as the epistemic bottom and citing the rung-6 correspondence. This is the rung Graphonomous could claim conformance on today."}]},{"id":"blk-39682","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44161","text":"Rung 8 — resource (affine ledger) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-39683","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44162","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/cost_tracker.ex"},{"id":"spn-44163","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44164","marks":["code"],"text":"budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-44165","text":" (line 167) enforces a "},{"id":"spn-44166","marks":["code"],"text":"$10/day"},{"id":"spn-44167","text":" cap — an "},{"id":"spn-44168","marks":["bold"],"text":"affine ledger"},{"id":"spn-44169","text":": spend is consumed and cannot go negative past the cap. The "},{"id":"spn-44170","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-44171","text":" (LRU + priority decay) is resource reclamation. This is the kernel's resource rung ("},{"id":"spn-44172","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-44173","text":", laws "},{"id":"spn-44174","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-44175","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-44176","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-44177","text":" emit the daily-budget remaining as a resource signal and name it with the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-44178","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-44179","text":", overspend → "},{"id":"spn-44180","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-44181","text":"), so unattended autonomy degrades gracefully via the same algebra the kernel uses."}]},{"id"